    <statement><p>Calculate the length of the path over the given interval.
<me>c(t) = (5 t^2, 10 t^3), \, 2 \le t \le 3</me></p>
<p><fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{2\cdot 10}{3\cdot 18}\mathopen{}\left(82^{\frac{3}{2}}-37^{\frac{3}{2}}\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>x = 5 t^2</m> and <m>y = 10 t^3</m>.  Hence <m>x' = 10 t</m> and <m>y' = 30 t^2</m>.  By the formula for the arc length we get
<me>S = \int ^{3} _{2} \sqrt{x'(t)^2 + y'(t)^2} \, dt = \int ^{3} _{2} \sqrt{100 t^2 + 900 t^4} \, dt = 10 \int ^{3} _{2} \sqrt{1 + 9 t^2} \, t \, dt</me>
Using the substitution <m>u = 1 + 9 t^2, \, du = 18 t \, dt</m> we obtain
<me>S = \frac{10}{18} \int ^{82} _{37} \sqrt{u} \, du = \frac{10}{18} \cdot \frac{2}{3} u^{3/2} \mid ^{82} _{37} = \frac{20}{54} ((82)^{3/2} - (37)^{3/2}) = 191.659</me>


</solution>
